{"title":"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alex, Mel, and Chelsea play a game that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rounds.  In each round there is a single winner, and the outcomes of the rounds are independent.  For each round the probability that Alex wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and Mel is twice as likely to win as Chelsea.  What is the probability that Alex wins three rounds, Mel wins two rounds, and Chelsea wins one round?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c43638c5498e4223723645631ea571d85c5918c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{5}{72}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"382\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the probability Mel wins and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the probability Chelsea wins, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/1578457a94ccf66cf036fcd136495ec820f2bc7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2c$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eee8532c66a51e5f6c377c77c073cfd42d7d19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+c=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />. From this we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917d7a9dbf8318eb7460b4f17b2d99668ecd9ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"51\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d274ec5c871229189b0795df73c145f6de4c1f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" />. For Alex to win three, Mel to win two, and Chelsea to win one, in that order, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa65737cb7db946623dde2f97bf4dd0d5694f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^3\\cdot3^2\\cdot6}=\\frac{1}{432}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />. Multiply this by the number of permutations (orders they can win) which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe555cd003538c7f07552fc16accf2319cce496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3,2,1}=\\frac{6!}{3!2!1!}=60.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"192\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b582e1d346e7d58fb28683bacf4579ee7b8dbc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{432}\\cdot60=\\frac{60}{432}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{36}}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability that Alex wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> , the probability that Mel wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> , and the probability that Chelsea wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> . There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/75569481af3db5bdcc1959c92cc955928d9c25ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways to pick the three games that Alex wins, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/50257e1113399bb38a23519393448f182d5f410d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways to pick 2 out of the 3 remaining games that Mel wins - theres <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4876d1ad73c7ce37e6e315e827eaa55a254301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{1}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> ways to see that Chelsea wins. Therefore, the number of ways is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec56da7d95841cd1833b2386b1f76addcede0eea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2^3}\\times\\frac{1}{3^2}\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\times\\binom{6}{3}\\times\\binom{3}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{36}}\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>~ youtube.com/@indianmathguy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I preview the concept that will be used in the first part of this video, and show why it's important \"Don't Memorize, Understand\". I adapt the solution method of an older problem to inform the solution of this one: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PO3XZaSchJc\">https://youtu.be/PO3XZaSchJc</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use a mix of rearrangements and probability. Since each game has an independent result, we can multiply the results. We know the probability that Alex wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> , the probability that Mel wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> , and the probability that Chelsea wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and we can just use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff4a295dfb811586bc4530eb95c621d0ca359ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6!}{2! * 3!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"39\" /> to find the total number of arrangements. We can then multiply this by the probability of each game being won, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967e149192e5c12d85ac838cb94a601bf613b9f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5}{36} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{36}}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~AncientKarnivore\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A\">2012 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017004418\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.405 seconds\nPreprocessor visited